:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]split_sidecar_config.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/split_sidecar_config.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-gu[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-gu/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Accept both shapes in the schema, parser, and doctor[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]dual_read[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]dual_read: teach the JSON schema, the sidecar config parser, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-generation validator, and the CI bootstrap tool to read the new [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]builtin/custom mapping while still accepting the legacy list, and add a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]doctor check that reports the migration and mis-bucketed roles.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Write and migrate every enabled project to the new shape[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]migrate_configs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after dual_read[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]migrate_configs: make sase repo init emit the two-bucket mapping, update[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the operator-facing guidance strings and docs examples, and migrate the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase, actstat, and bob-cli project configs to the new shape.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Remove the legacy list form[/bold #D7AFFF]                                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]drop_legacy[dim] · [dim][/dim]after migrate_configs[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]drop_legacy: delete the legacy list branch from the schema, parser, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory validator, and CI bootstrap tool so repos.sidecar is a closed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]builtin/custom object, and land it as a breaking change.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-gu","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","phase_bead_id":"sase-gu.1","reasoning_effort":"medium","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-9ad154bb6b729e86e655fb8037e6350e","started_at":"2026-08-07T13:35:31.291783+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.sase-gu","bbugyi200.athena.sase-gu.1","bbugyi200.athena.sase-gu.2","bbugyi200.athena.sase-gu.3","bbugyi200.athena.sase-gu.land"]}
